# options of macOS or GNU that are not in the synopsis (-A -b -B -c -d -g -h -I -l -m -n -P -t): a usage error here
-b
-A t
-B 512 t
-c t
-d 1 t
-l t
-m t
-P t
-t 1 t
-h t
-g t
-I x t
-n t
# a file that was counted under one operand is counted again under the next here, so that every file operand is written (the standard: "implementation-defined whether a file that occurs under one file operand is counted for other file operands", and -a does not decide whether a file operand is written); all three references count it once for all the operands
-a h/one h/two
h/one h/two
